# docs-skills — four documentation skills

This project defines four documentation skills. When the user mentions docs-create, docs-analyze,
docs-manage or docs-automate — or describes the job one of them covers — apply that skill definition
from `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, then only the reference files its routing table points at.

- docs-create   — documentation that does not exist yet (from a site, a repo, a migration, or an idea)
- docs-analyze  — what is wrong, starting from real numbers, through to the applied fix
- docs-manage   — the rulebook for what a page says and what the site around it does
- docs-automate — drift guards, CI checks, event handlers, alerts and monitors

Every skill works on a plain docs folder with nothing connected. A `markdown-lsp` server or a
connected Docsbook workspace makes them faster and sharper, never different.

Optional cloud transport: mcp add --transport http https://docsbook.io/api/mcp/server
